# What each recorded bench read (T174 D5, ci/simreads.py, written by `ci/sims.sh --record NAME`): the files below are its key, and
# ci/sims.deps says `@reads` for it. Lines: <file> a tracked file it opened | ?<path> looked for, not there (adding it changes the run)
# | @<dir> listed (adding or removing a file there changes the run). A run that reads more extends the runner's copy of the record in
# its cache, so the key follows the run; this file is what the plan and the lint see. Do not edit by hand.
atari_led:
  cores/atari800/layer2_atari800.v
  cores/atari800/sim/led/run.sh
  cores/atari800/sim/led/tb_sio_led.v
